def expected_utility(outcomes):
    return sum(p * u for p, u in outcomes)

def treatments(harm_rate):
    return {
        "standard": [(0.60, 70), (0.40, 20)],                      # cured / not cured.
        "new": [(0.80 - harm_rate, 90), (0.20, 20), (harm_rate, -100)],   # cured / not / harmed.
    }

for harm in (0.02, 0.05, 0.10):
    eus = {name: round(expected_utility(o), 1) for name, o in treatments(harm).items()}
    best = max(eus, key=eus.get)
    print(harm, eus, "->", best)
# 0.02 {'standard': 50.0, 'new': 72.2} -> new
# 0.05 {'standard': 50.0, 'new': 66.5} -> new
# 0.10 {'standard': 50.0, 'new': 57.0} -> new
```

The choice holds across this harm range. Try a patient who values harm at -600 instead of -100, and watch where it flips.

